.TH fforth 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
fforth \- a Forth interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fforth
[\fIfile\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fforth
is a small indirect-threaded Forth by David Given, written for FUZIX.
It implements most of the ANS Forth core word set and passes most of the
Hayes conformance tests.
.PP
Run with no arguments it reads from the terminal and answers
.B ok
after each line it likes.  Given files, it reads those first.
.PP
.B bye
leaves.
.SH NOTES
This is a complete language on the machine, alongside BBC BASIC, the C
compiler and the MMBasic translator.  It is the smallest of them and the
quickest to start.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bbcbasic (1),
.BR cc (1),
.BR dc (1)
